# Build-context exclusions for the Containerfile (ADR 0022 section 2).
#
# The PAC builder clones the pushed commit, so on the hub these paths are
# absent anyway; the list matters for local `podman build` runs, where they
# would bloat the context and could leak local build output into the image.
# Each stage rebuilds what it needs from source: the rust stage compiles into
# a fresh target/, and the admin stage runs npm ci and npm run build.

# ADR 0022 section 2.
target/
.git/
admin/node_modules/
admin/dist/

# Local test output that has no place in an image.
admin/playwright-report/
admin/test-results/
e2e-logs/

# Local environment files can hold credentials; never send them to a builder.
.env
.env.*

# Personal Loco configuration overrides. loco-rs 1.2.0 deep-merges
# config/<env>.local.yaml over config/<env>.yaml (config/mod.rs,
# `from_folder`), and .gitignore keeps them out of commits because they may
# hold local credentials. The rust stage copies config/ into the image, so a
# local `podman build` would otherwise ship such a file and let it override
# config/production.yaml.
config/local.yaml
config/*.local.yaml
